# code-is-decision-vs — D4 PARTIAL-split author-ValueSet routing fixture.
library "Code Is Decision VS".

// Like `code-is-decision` (a DECISION-bearing library that partial-splits), but
// it ALSO carries an EXTERNAL author terminology (`valueset is`) consumed by a
// `coded from` concept — NOT just local `code is`. D4 pins that BOTH the local
// CodeSystem AND the author ValueSet's canonical route onto the `<source>
// Concepts` Library's depends-on (the terminology relocates into Concepts under
// the partial split), and that NEITHER lands on the Root.

terminology "GI Referral Reasons":
- valueset is `http://example.org/crl/code-is-decision-vs/ValueSet/gi-referral-reasons`.

concept "Adult Patient":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `adult-18-or-older`.

concept "Referral Reason":
- type is Observation.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- coded from "GI Referral Reasons".

activity "Refer to GI":
- request CPGServiceRequest.

decision "Triage Crohns":
- when "Adult Patient" then recommend activity "Refer to GI".
